WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.448
Experiments use two data types.

00:00:03.528 --> 00:00:06.976
First,

00:00:07.056 --> 00:00:10.504
synthetic sparse precision matrices from
Scikit-learn: a small fifteen-by-fifteen case to visualize posteriors,

00:00:10.584 --> 00:00:14.032
and a thirty-dimensional setting with fifteen to
forty-five samples for edge recovery,

00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:17.560
averaged over ten ground-truth matrices.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.088
Second,

00:00:21.168 --> 00:00:24.616
a real colorectal-cancer dataset with six clinical
variables and three hundred twelve

00:00:24.696 --> 00:00:28.144
gene-expression measurements across one hundred
ninety patients,

00:00:28.224 --> 00:00:31.672
inferring only the relevant sub-blocks of the
precision matrix.
